Z||000000||ponya||01-25-2001||08:01 PM||||Does anyone know what I can use to clean the contacts on the circuit board where the lights screw into. My son who owned this car before me, tells me he has changed the bulbs on the circuit, but only half stay on all the time and the other half come on when they want to. I think the contacts need to be cleaned. Just want to use something that wont hurt the board causing more problems than I have now. Any suggestions appreciated,  Bob||||reg||1
Z||000001||MikeSchaefer||01-25-2001||08:04 PM||||Radio Shack sells a spray called "electrical contact cleaner" Which works quite well, use a little file to get the oxidation off, then spray the contacts down with the cleaner.  I haven't done this on my Fiero, but it worked well in my Delorean.<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||01-25-2001||08:16 PM||||  You can use a pencil eraser on the actual contacts themselves. It works really well.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
